How would you interpret a large standard error for a regression coefficient?

A large standard error suggests that the estimate of the regression coefficient is imprecise, indicating high variability in the data or multicollinearity.

Polynomial Regression
What is polynomial regression?

Polynomial regression is an extension of linear regression where the relationship between the independent variable and the dependent variable is modeled as an nth-degree polynomial.

When is polynomial regression used?

Polynomial regression is used when the relationship between the variables is nonlinear, but a polynomial curve can describe the relationship well.

How does the intercept in a regression model provide context for the relationship between variables?

The intercept indicates the starting point of the model when all predictor variables are zero, providing context for the base level of the dependent variable.

How can heteroscedasticity be identified in residual plots, and why is it important to address it?

Heteroscedasticity can be identified in residual plots if the spread of residuals increases or decreases with the value of the independent variable. It is important to address it to improve model reliability.

