Why is it important to scale variables in Multiple Linear Regression?

Scaling variables ensures that all predictors contribute equally to the model, preventing any variable from dominating due to its larger scale.

How does polynomial regression differ from linear regression?

Polynomial regression fits a curved line to the data, while linear regression fits a straight line. Polynomial regression can model nonlinear relationships.

