Can polynomial regression be applied to multiple variables?

Yes, polynomial regression can be extended to multiple variables by adding interaction terms and higher-degree terms for each predictor.

What are the limitations of polynomial regression?

Polynomial regression can lead to overfitting if the degree of the polynomial is too high. It also can be sensitive to outliers.

